Q: typeorm not supports &#39;vector&#39; type directly for hybrid search using postgresql A: <p>I was facing the same problem and figured out two options to do this.</p>
<p><strong>1.</strong> Add the column you want to save vector in as a text type. Then run a query something like this:</p>
<pre><code>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;  

ALTER TABLE question_vectors  
ADD COLUMN question_vector_vec vector(1536);  

UPDATE question_vectors  
SET question_vector_vec = question_vector::vector;  

ALTER TABLE question_vectors  
DROP COLUMN question_vector;
</code></pre>
<p>The entity file had this field as</p>
<pre><code>@Column({
    type: 'text',
    nullable: true,
    // Tell TypeORM to use the exact type from the database
    transformer: {
      to: (value: number[] | string | null) =&gt; {
        if (value === null || value === undefined) return null;
        if (typeof value === 'string') return value;
        return `[${value.join(',')}]`;
      },
      from: (value: string | null) =&gt; {
        if (value === null || value === undefined) return null;
        return value;
      },
    },
  })
  @ApiProperty({
    description: 'Vector representation of the question text (1536 dimensions)',
  })
  question_vector: string | null;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>2.</strong> Run migrations for updating as this way you wont have to run the query again and again.</p>
<p>Example:</p>
<pre><code>import { MigrationInterface, QueryRunner } from 'typeorm';

export class AddVectorColumn1725555555555 implements MigrationInterface {
  name = 'AddVectorColumn1725555555555';

  public async up(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    // Ensure pgvector extension is available
    await queryRunner.query(`CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector`);


    await queryRunner.query(
      `ALTER TABLE &quot;question_vectors&quot; ADD COLUMN &quot;question_vector&quot; vector(1536)`
    );
  }

  public async down(queryRunner: QueryRunner): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    await queryRunner.query(
      `ALTER TABLE &quot;question_vectors&quot; DROP COLUMN &quot;question_vector&quot;`
    );
  }
}
</code></pre>

